      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Histologic and scanning electron-microscopic investigation of myocardium specimens from patients who had died of various diseases demonstrated cardiomyocyte dissociation which was more common for coronary heart disease accompanied by myocardial infarction and cardiac fibrillation. Consistent morphologic pattern and clinical manifestability of the process permit the establishment of cardiomyocyte dissociation as a specific form of myocardial affection."},
